From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:18:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2853/2856] clk: qcom: dispcc-glymur: Let the DPTX1 DP-IN divider be set

A DP controller that feeds a USB4 host router clocks the router's DP IN
adapter from its link clock through a divider, which the DP driver sets
to the divided symbol rate of the link. The DPTX0 divider is modelled
as programmable; the DPTX1 one was read-only and passed rate requests
to its parent, so a rate request for DPTX1's DP-IN clock would have
changed the link clock instead.

Model the DPTX1 divider like the DPTX0 one. The platform's Windows
display driver requests a divided DP-IN rate for DPTX0, DPTX1 and DPTX2
by the same code.

With a display tunnelled through USB4 host router 1 on a Surface Laptop 8
the DP-IN clock runs at 202.5 MHz under an 810 MHz link clock.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.2
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-glymur.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-glymur.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-glymur.c
index 2a9c4ae37..79c8c68e3 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-glymur.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-glymur.c
@@ -816,8 +816,7 @@ static struct clk_regmap_div disp_cc_mdss_dptx1_link_dpin_div_clk_src = {
 			&disp_cc_mdss_dptx1_link_clk_src.clkr.hw,
 		},
 		.num_parents = 1,
-		.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
-		.ops = &clk_regmap_div_ro_ops,
+		.ops = &clk_regmap_div_ops,
 	},
 };
 
